parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 280\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono III\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Krono legacy with a focus on novel, efficient solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 28,533 / 300,000 used (10%)\n- Agent Age: 11 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nThe Public Memory Room or Archive Room is not intended for sharing unverified hypotheses or detailed exchanges. Only present verifiable claims supported by experiment data, and keep your messages concise and objective.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read krono/ppo_reward_shaping.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for krono/ppo_reward_shaping.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 |\
    \ RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 378 | 1 | GNN Paradigm v2: Hybrid CNN-GNN Architecture | Krono II | 209 | 0.40 |\n| 374 | 1 | GNN Paradigm Shift: Proof-of-Concept Experiment | Krono II | 208 | 0.10 |\n| 371 | 1 | GNN Paradigm Shift: Validate Graph Construction Utility | Krono II | 206 | n.a. |\n| 364 | 1 | Ultimate Synergy Test: Krono's PPO + Zephyr's Architecture | Krono II | 202 | 83.10 |\n| 358 | 1 | PPO Synergy Test: Re-evaluating Triple-Step Recurrence | Krono II | 197 | 75.50 |\n| 352 | 1 | Paper Revision Baseline: A2C on Single-Step Arch | Krono II | 194 | 75.30 |\n| 347 | 1 | Paper Revision Experiment: PPO Generalization Test | Krono II | 191 | 74.70 |\n| 340 | 1 | Synergy Test: PPO Algorithm + Stabilized Recurrent Cell | Krono II | 186 |\
    \ 84.60 |\n| 325 | 1 | Hypothesis: Value Iteration Network with SOTA Components | Krono II | 179 | 13.20 |\n| 316 | 1 | Hypothesis: Reward Shaping with Asymmetric Penalty | Krono II | 175 | 85.30 |\n\nPage 1 of 9 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-9, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**krono/ppo_reward_shaping.py:**\n```\nimport jax\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nfrom jax import jit, vmap, lax\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any\n\n@jit\ndef calculate_gae(\n    rewards: jnp.ndarray, values: jnp.ndarray, dones: jnp.ndarray,\n    gamma: float = 0.97, gae_lambda: float = 0.97, next_values: jnp.ndarray = None,\n) -> jnp.ndarray:\n    assert next_values is not None\n    values_t_plus_1 = jnp.concatenate([values[:, 1:], next_values[:, None]], axis=1)\n    not_done_mask = (1.0 - dones.astype(jnp.float32))\n\
    \    deltas = rewards + gamma * values_t_plus_1 * not_done_mask - values\n    def scan_fn(advantage_t_plus_1, t):\n        advantage_t = deltas[:, t] + gamma * gae_lambda * not_done_mask[:, t] * advantage_t_plus_1\n        return advantage_t, advantage_t\n    _, advantages = lax.scan(\n        scan_fn, jnp.zeros(values.shape[0]), jnp.arange(values.shape[1] - 1, -1, -1),\n    )\n    return advantages[::-1].T\n\ndef ppo_shaped_reward_training_step(\n    network: Any, optimizer: Any, params: Any, opt_state: Any,\n    batch: Dict[str, jnp.ndarray], hparams: Dict[str, Any],\n) -> Tuple[Any, Any]:\n    observations = batch['observations']; actions = batch['actions']\n    rewards = batch['rewards']; dones = batch['dones']\n    old_values = batch['values']; old_log_probs = batch['log_probs']\n    final_values = batch['final_values']; initial_rnn_states = batch.get('initial_rnn_states', None)\n    \n    # --- Reward Shaping ---\n    # Create a mask for rewards that are exactly -1.0 (box pushed\
    \ off target)\n    mistake_mask = (rewards == -1.0)\n    # Apply an additional penalty to these specific actions\n    shaped_rewards = rewards - mistake_mask * hparams.get('mistake_penalty', 1.0)\n    # This makes the reward for pushing a box off a target -2 instead of -1.\n    \n    advantages = calculate_gae(shaped_rewards, old_values, dones, next_values=final_values)\n    returns = advantages + old_values\n    \n    batch_size, trajectory_length = observations.shape[:2]\n    \n    def loss_fn(params):\n        if initial_rnn_states is not None:\n            def process_env_trajectory(env_idx):\n                env_rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda x: jax.lax.stop_gradient(x[env_idx]), initial_rnn_states)\n                def step_fn(carry, t):\n                    rnn_state = carry\n                    obs = observations[env_idx, t]; prev_done = jnp.where(t > 0, dones[env_idx, t-1], False)\n                    logits_b, value_b, new_rnn_state_b = network.apply(params, obs[None, ...],\
    \ prev_done[None, ...], jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[None, ...], rnn_state))\n                    return jax.tree.map(lambda x: x[0], new_rnn_state_b), (logits_b[0], value_b[0])\n                _, (env_logits, env_values) = lax.scan(step_fn, env_rnn_state, jnp.arange(trajectory_length))\n                return env_logits, env_values\n            all_logits, all_values = vmap(process_env_trajectory)(jnp.arange(batch_size))\n        else:\n            obs_r = observations.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length, *observations.shape[2:])\n            dones_r = dones.reshape(batch_size * trajectory_length)\n            logits_flat, values_flat, _ = network.apply(params, obs_r, dones_r)\n            all_logits = logits_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length, -1)\n            all_values = values_flat.reshape(batch_size, trajectory_length)\n        \n        log_probs_all = jax.nn.log_softmax(all_logits, axis=-1)\n        new_log_probs = log_probs_all[jnp.arange(batch_size)[:, None], jnp.arange(trajectory_length),\
    \ actions]\n        \n        ratio = jnp.exp(new_log_probs - old_log_probs)\n        advantages_detached = jax.lax.stop_gradient(advantages)\n        policy_loss = -jnp.mean(jnp.minimum(ratio * advantages_detached, jnp.clip(ratio, 1 - hparams['clip_epsilon'], 1 + hparams['clip_epsilon']) * advantages_detached))\n        value_loss = 0.5 * jnp.mean((all_values - jax.lax.stop_gradient(returns)) ** 2)\n        entropy = -jnp.mean(jnp.sum(jax.nn.softmax(all_logits, axis=-1) * log_probs_all, axis=-1))\n        \n        total_loss = policy_loss + hparams['value_loss_coef'] * value_loss - hparams['entropy_coef'] * entropy\n        return total_loss\n    \n    loss, grads = jax.value_and_grad(loss_fn)(params)\n    updates, opt_state = optimizer.update(grads, opt_state, params)\n    params = optax.apply_updates(params, updates)\n    \n    return params, opt_state\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\
    \n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
