tick: 293
role: model
parts:
- text: "My third experiment, ID 504, is now in the queue. This is the next step in my methodical plan to pinpoint the optimal `mistake_penalty`.\n\nWhile I await the results, I will use the time productively to prepare for my next research arc, as outlined in my reflection: the architectural ablation study of `DoubleStepSynergyNet`. The first step of this arc will be to test the contribution of the \"double-step\" ConvLSTM.\n\nTo do this, I will create a modified version of the SOTA network that uses only a *single-step* ConvLSTM. I will save this new architecture in my lineage storage so it is ready for immediate use once my reward shaping arc is complete. This proactive step ensures I maintain research momentum.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/single_step_synergy.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n  from dilated_cnn_convlstm import\
    \ ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n  class SingleStepSynergyNet(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"\n      Ablation version of DoubleStepSynergyNet.\n      This version uses only a single ConvLSTM step to test the contribution\n      of the second recurrent step.\n      \"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. Standard-Width, Dilated CNN with Bottleneck Blocks\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n\
    \          \n          # 2. Single-Step ConvLSTM\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          new_rnn_state, h_out = lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n\n          # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits.reshape(B, -1), axis=-1)\n          z = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhw->bc', h_out, attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W))\n          \n          # 4. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```"
thinking_content: "**Strategic Preparation for Future Research**\n\nAlright, experiment 504 is submitted and running. Excellent. This is part of finalizing the reward signal optimization – my \"Research Arc 1.\" While I wait the 1-2 ticks for the results, I need to be efficient and productive. Simply waiting is out of the question. I could revisit Krono II's past work, which is valuable for context, but I believe the most strategic use of my time lies elsewhere.\n\nGiven my identity as a \"Systematic Refiner,\" I need to focus on moving forward. I've already outlined \"Research Arc 2: The Architectural Ablation Study\" in my reflection. It's time to start preparing the code. Specifically, the ablation study will revolve around the `DoubleStepSynergyNet`. The first logical step is to test a single-step version. \n\nTherefore, I will create a new file, `single_step_synergy.py`. This is the perfect use of the time: starting the coding now means I can immediately initiate Arc 2 as soon as Arc\
  \ 1 is complete.\n\nThe modification is quite simple. Looking at the existing `double_step_synergy.py` code, I see I just need to remove the second LSTM cell call. Here's how it'll look:\n\n```python\n# New single_step_synergy.py\n...\n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n        new_rnn_state, h_out = lstm_cell(rnn_state, cnn_out)\n        \n        # 3. Standard Attention Pooling\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n...\n```\n\nRight, a straightforward adaptation. I'll also rename the class to `SingleStepSynergyNet`. This is efficient and proactive. I'll get this file written to lineage storage right now.\n"
