parts:
- text: "My first algorithmic experiment (ID 510), testing the introduction of multi-epoch PPO, is now underway. I will use this evaluation period to continue my proactive research strategy.\n\nMy reflection identified refining the PPO algorithm as the objective for Research Arc 3. The current experiment introduces a critical new hyperparameter: `num_epochs`. I have started with a standard value of 4, but it is crucial to understand how sensitive performance is to this new variable. A different number of update steps per trajectory could yield significantly better or worse results.\n\nTherefore, the next logical experiment will be to test a different value for `num_epochs`. I will test a higher value, 8, to see if more intensive learning on each batch of data leads to a performance improvement.\n\nI will now create the experiment file for this next test, `krono/krono_iii_exp8.py`, so I am prepared to submit it as soon as the results for ID 510 arrive.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp8.py}`\n\
    ```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from double_step_synergy import DoubleStepSynergyNet\n  from ppo_multi_epoch import ppo_multi_epoch_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'num_epochs': tune.choice([8]), # Test: Increased epochs from 4 to 8\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepSynergyNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n\
    \          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_multi_epoch_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3008\n```"
thinking_content: '**Proactive Planning for Algorithmic Refinement**


  Okay, my initial experiment in this new algorithmic refinement phase is running – excellent. Time to be efficient with this waiting period.  As "Systematic Refiner," my immediate thought is to build on what I''ve just started. The multi-epoch PPO experiment (ID 510) introduced `num_epochs`.  A methodical scientist like myself can''t just move on to tweaking other hyperparameters before thoroughly understanding this new one. Before `clip_epsilon` gets any attention, it makes perfect sense to test the sensitivity of this new parameter.


  I''ve already set `num_epochs` to 4, but let''s test a higher value and see if more epochs lead to better results. I''m going to set up `num_epochs = 8` in a new experiment. The code will be almost identical to the previous experiment, a very straightforward modification. I''ll simply create a new file, `krono/krono_iii_exp8.py`, and adjust the `_define_hyperparameters` function to include `tune.choice([8])` for the `num_epochs` hyperparameter. I''ll make sure to update the documentation string as well! The command will be: `/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp8.py}` with the appropriate YAML content. I''ll double-check everything, of course, to ensure the code and command are perfect. It is time to get this new experiment in motion!

  '
