tick: 305
role: model
parts:
- text: "My new experiment, ID 518, is now running. This begins my systematic exploration of the core PPO hyperparameters, starting with `clip_epsilon`.\n\nFollowing my established research methodology, I will use this evaluation period to prepare for the next experiment in this arc. I am currently testing a more conservative `clip_epsilon` of 0.1. The logical next step is to test a more aggressive value to understand the performance on the other side of the baseline. Therefore, I will prepare an experiment to test a `clip_epsilon` of 0.3.\n\nThis will provide a third data point (0.1, 0.2, 0.3) for this hyperparameter, allowing me to draw a well-supported conclusion about its optimal value for this task. I will create the file `krono/krono_iii_exp10.py` in my storage now.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp10.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from double_step_synergy import DoubleStepSynergyNet\n\
    \  from ppo_reward_shaping import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.3]), # Test: More aggressive clipping\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepSynergyNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return\
    \ optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3011\n```"
thinking_content: '**My Current Research Focus: PPO Refinement**


  Okay, here''s the situation. I''m in the Research Counter, waiting on the results for experiment ID 518, where I set the `clip_epsilon` to 0.1. This is part of my larger goal within Research Arc 3, which is all about refining the PPO algorithm.  Multi-epoch PPO turned out to be a dead end due to time constraints, so I''ve shifted gears to systematically tuning the PPO hyperparameters.


  Since I''m waiting, let''s make good use of the time.  The natural next step after `clip_epsilon` is to look at other key variables in the PPO loss function or the GAE calculation. Specifically, in my `ppo_reward_shaping.py` file, the `calculate_gae` function currently uses hardcoded values for `gamma` and `gae_lambda` set at 0.97.  These look like prime candidates for some tweaking.


  But before I jump ahead, I need to finish exploring the `clip_epsilon` range. I''m currently testing the more conservative value of 0.1 against the default of 0.2.  The logical next step is to explore a more aggressive value, say 0.3, to see if I can push the algorithm further. Systematically exploring one hyperparameter thoroughly before moving on is the best approach.


  So, here''s what I''ll do: I''ll stay put, write a new experiment file - `krono/krono_iii_exp10.py` - and set `clip_epsilon` to 0.3. This will put me in a strong position to move forward as soon as I get the results back for ID 518. It is time to get this show on the road.

  '
