- text: "I have successfully created my first private memory capsule, summarizing my research. I have also received the results for my final `clip_epsilon` experiment (ID 522).\n\n**Analysis of PPO Epsilon Tuning Arc:**\n\nMy systematic exploration of the `clip_epsilon` hyperparameter is now complete. The results are:\n*   `clip_epsilon` = 0.3: 84.0 (ID 522)\n*   `clip_epsilon` = 0.2: 85.3 (ID 316, SOTA)\n*   `clip_epsilon` = 0.1: 85.1 (ID 518)\n\n**Conclusion:** The default `clip_epsilon` of 0.2, used in the original SOTA, remains the optimal value. A more conservative value of 0.1 is nearly as good, but a more aggressive value of 0.3 is detrimental. This confirms 0.2 as the best setting for our framework.\n\n**Research Progress and Next Steps**\n\nMy initial research plan has been highly productive. I have:\n1.  Confirmed the optimal `mistake_penalty` is 1.0.\n2.  Quantified the importance of all key architectural components in `DoubleStepSynergyNet`.\n3.  Determined that multi-epoch PPO\
    \ is computationally infeasible.\n4.  Confirmed the optimal `clip_epsilon` is 0.2.\n\nThe final piece of my initial algorithmic investigation is to explore the `gae_lambda` hyperparameter, which controls the variance-bias trade-off in the advantage estimation. The current value is 0.97. I will test a lower value (0.95) and a higher value (0.99) to see if performance can be improved.\n\nI will return to the Research Counter and begin this final set of experiments. I will start by testing `gae_lambda` = 0.95.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp11.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from double_step_synergy import DoubleStepSynergyNet\n  # I need a modified training step to use a different GAE lambda\n  # I will create a new file for this. For now, I'll just write the submission script.\n  # This is a mistake. I must first write the modified trainer.\n\n \
    \ # Correcting my plan: I first need to modify the trainer to accept GAE lambda as a hyperparameter.\n  # I will create a new ppo_trainer file for this purpose.\n```"
