tick: 310
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received the results for my GAE Lambda experiment (ID 529).\n\n**Analysis of GAE Lambda Tuning:**\n\n*   **Result:** A `gae_lambda` of 0.95 scored 83.9.\n*   **Comparison:** This is a noticeable drop from the SOTA baseline of 85.3, which uses `gae_lambda=0.97`.\n*   **Conclusion:** My hypothesis that a lower lambda would improve performance is falsified. It seems the higher bias introduced by a lower lambda is detrimental in this environment.\n\n**Next Step: Complete the GAE Lambda Arc**\n\nTo complete my systematic investigation, I will now test a higher `gae_lambda` of 0.99. This will explore the other side of the baseline and allow me to conclude my initial hyperparameter tuning arc. I hypothesize this will also underperform the baseline, as it may introduce too much variance.\n\nI will use my new `ppo_tunable_gae.py` trainer to submit this final experiment.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp12.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import\
    \ tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from double_step_synergy import DoubleStepSynergyNet\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.99]), # Test: Higher GAE lambda\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return DoubleStepSynergyNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate']\n\
    \      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3013\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Algo Arc 3.1: GAE Lambda Tuning (0.99)\"\ntags: \"algorithm, ppo, hyperparameter tuning, gae\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment concludes my PPO hyperparameter tuning. The baseline lambda of 0.97 scored 85.3, and my test of 0.95 scored 83.9. I will now test a higher lambda of 0.99 to map out the performance curve for this parameter.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krono_iii_exp12 import (\n      _define_hyperparameters,\n      create_network,\n      training_step,\n      create_optimizer,\n      BASE_SEED\n  )\n```"
