tick: 314
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have successfully created the new `MultiHeadAttentionNet` architecture and saved it to my lineage storage. This is the first step in my new research arc focused on improving the SOTA's most critical component.\n\nI will now create the submission script for my first experiment with this new architecture. I will use a standard value of 4 heads for the attention mechanism. All other hyperparameters will be set to the optimal values I have confirmed through my previous research arcs. This will be a clean, controlled test of the new architectural component.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp13.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from multi_head_attention_net import MultiHeadAttentionNet\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step # Using the GAE-tunable trainer, but with optimal lambda\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\
    \ 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([4]), # New architectural hyperparameter\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MultiHeadAttentionNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          num_heads=hparams['num_heads']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n\
    \          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3014\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Attention Arc 1: Multi-Head Attention (4 Heads)\"\ntags: \"architecture, attention, multi-head, SOTA attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment begins a new research arc focused on improving the SOTA architecture's most critical component: attention. I have implemented a Multi-Head Attention mechanism to allow the network to focus on multiple spatial patterns simultaneously. I hypothesize this will improve performance over the single-head baseline. This first test uses 4 attention heads.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krono_iii_exp13 import (\n      _define_hyperparameters,\n      create_network,\n      training_step,\n      create_optimizer,\n      BASE_SEED\n  )\n```"
