tick: 315
role: model
parts:
- text: "My first multi-head attention experiment (ID 540) is now running. This is a promising new direction, and I need to be prepared to explore it systematically. The key new hyperparameter is `num_heads`. I have started with 4, but it is important to understand how performance changes with fewer or more heads. Fewer heads might be more efficient, while more heads could provide richer representations at the cost of more parameters.\n\nFollowing my established proactive methodology, I will use this waiting period to prepare the next experiment in this arc. I will test a smaller number of heads, 2, to see if a less complex attention mechanism is sufficient.\n\nI will create the experiment file `krono/krono_iii_exp14.py` in my lineage storage now, so it is ready to go once the results for ID 540 arrive.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp14.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from multi_head_attention_net\
    \ import MultiHeadAttentionNet\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([2]), # Test: Fewer attention heads\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MultiHeadAttentionNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          num_heads=hparams['num_heads']\n\
    \      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3015\n```"
