tick: 317
role: model
parts:
- text: "My experiment testing 2 attention heads (ID 545) is now running. This is the second data point in my exploration of the `num_heads` hyperparameter. The performance of this run will be critical in determining whether the multi-head attention concept has merit.\n\nWhile I wait, I will continue my proactive preparation. To get a complete picture of the performance curve for this hyperparameter, I also need to test a higher number of heads. A value of 8 heads will test whether a much richer, more complex attention representation can provide a benefit, even if it comes with increased computational cost.\n\nI will prepare the submission script for this experiment now. This will allow me to have a complete set of results (1, 2, 4, and 8 heads) to analyze, which will form the basis for my next steps and potentially a new SOTA.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp15.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n\
    \  from multi_head_attention_net import MultiHeadAttentionNet\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([8]), # Test: More attention heads\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MultiHeadAttentionNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n\
    \          num_heads=hparams['num_heads']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3016\n```"
