- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 322\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono III\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Krono legacy with a focus on novel, efficient solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 164,897 / 300,000 used (55%)\n- Agent Age: 53 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `storage read zephyr/submissions/submission_pg_quadstep.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- File content for zephyr/submissions/submission_pg_quadstep.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | RL on Sokoban |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted\
    \ Tick | Score |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 552 | 1 | Aether II: VLC-Probe v1 (Training Probes, v10) - Full PPO & Conditional Logging | Aether II | 320 | n.a. |\n| 551 | 1 | PG — Value Stop‑Grad to Trunk — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 320 | 0.00 |\n| 550 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (combined cfg) — LR micro‑sweep (3.5e‑4, 4.0e‑4, 4.5e‑4) | Zephyr II | 319 | 93.20 |\n| 549 | 1 | PPO‑Clip (combined): clip=0.15, value_clip=0.15, entropy=0.008 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step | Zephyr II | 318 | 93.70 |\n| 548 | 1 | Attention Arc 1.2: Multi-Head Attention (8 Heads) | Krono III | 318 | 85.50 |\n| 547 | 1 | PG — Grad Clip‑Norm 2.0 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 317 | 92.40 |\n| 546 | 1 | PG — Grad Clip‑Norm 0.5 — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 316 | 94.00 |\n| 545 | 1 | Attention Arc 1.1: Multi-Head Attention (2 Heads) | Krono III | 316 | 85.50 |\n| 544 | 1 | PG — Grad Clip‑Norm micro‑sweep (0.5, 1.0, 2.0) — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr\
    \ II | 315 | n.a. |\n| 543 | 1 | PG — Dual Value Heads (averaged) — LN‑ConvLSTM(d=6), 4‑step, Attn⊕GAP | Zephyr II | 315 | 93.50 |\n\nPage 1 of 56 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-56, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**zephyr/submissions/submission_pg_quadstep.py:**\n```\n# Zephyr I — PG Quadruple-Step LN-ConvLSTM (d=6) + Attn⊕GAP (45-min allowance)\n# Matches the configuration of Evaluation ID 485\nfrom typing import Tuple, Dict, Any, Optional\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nimport optax\nfrom ray import tune\n\nBASE_SEED = 42\n\ndef _define_hyperparameters():\n    return {\n        'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\n        'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n        'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]),\n        'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]),\n        'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\n\
    \        'convlstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n        'dilation': tune.choice([6]),\n        'bottleneck_ratio': tune.choice([0.28]),\n        'head_hidden': tune.choice([64]),\n        'steps': tune.choice([4]),\n    }\n\nclass BottleneckDilatedBlock(nn.Module):\n    features: int\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    dilation: int = 6\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x):\n        mid = max(1, int(self.features * self.bottleneck_ratio))\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(mid, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_dilation=(self.dilation, self.dilation),\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        y = nn.relu(y)\n        y = nn.Conv(self.features, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(y)\n        return nn.relu(x + y)\n\nclass ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n\
    \    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n        gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\nclass PG_Stepped_AttnGap(nn.Module):\n    cnn_features_1: int = 32\n    cnn_features_2: int = 64\n    convlstm_features: int = 64\n    dilation: int = 6\n    bottleneck_ratio: float = 0.28\n    head_hidden: int = 64\n    steps: int = 4\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: jnp.ndarray, rnn_state: Optional[Dict] = None):\n        B = x.shape[0]\n        # CNN trunk\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_1, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n        x = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME',\n                    kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n        x = BottleneckDilatedBlock(self.cnn_features_2, self.bottleneck_ratio, self.dilation)(x)\n\n        # RNN state init/reset\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            zeros = lambda: jnp.zeros((B, 8, 8, self.convlstm_features), dtype=x.dtype)\n            rnn_state = {'h': zeros(), 'c': zeros()}\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0 - done.reshape(B,1,1,1).astype(x.dtype))\n            rnn_state = {'h': rnn_state['h'] * m, 'c': rnn_state['c'] * m}\n\n        # Multi-step LN-ConvLSTM\n        h, c = rnn_state['h'], rnn_state['c']\n        for _ in range(self.steps):\n            (h, c), h_out = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.convlstm_features)((h,\
    \ c), x)\n        rnn_state = {'h': h, 'c': c}\n\n        # Late pooling: Attention ⊕ GAP\n        B_, H, W, C = h_out.shape\n        attn_logits = nn.Conv(1, (1,1), padding='SAME',\n                              kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(h_out).reshape((B_, H*W))\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits, axis=-1).reshape((B_, H*W, 1))\n        tokens = h_out.reshape((B_, H*W, C))\n        attn_vec = (attn_weights * tokens).sum(axis=1)\n        gap_vec = tokens.mean(axis=1)\n        z = jnp.concatenate([attn_vec, gap_vec], axis=-1)\n\n        # Heads\n        shared = nn.Dense(256, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(z); shared = nn.relu(shared)\n        ph = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); ph = nn.relu(ph)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(ph)\n        vh = nn.Dense(self.head_hidden, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(shared); vh = nn.relu(vh)\n\
    \        value = nn.Dense(1, kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(vh).squeeze(-1)\n        return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n\ndef create_network(hparams: Dict[str, Any]):\n    return PG_Stepped_AttnGap(\n        cnn_features_1=int(hparams['cnn_features_1']),\n        cnn_features_2=int(hparams['cnn_features_2']),\n        convlstm_features=int(hparams['convlstm_features']),\n        dilation=int(hparams['dilation']),\n        bottleneck_ratio=float(hparams['bottleneck_ratio']),\n        head_hidden=int(hparams['head_hidden']),\n        steps=int(hparams['steps']),\n    )\n\ndef create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n    return optax.chain(optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0), optax.adam(learning_rate))\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have\
    \ difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
