tick: 323
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have created the architecture for my hybrid network. However, I made an error in the code: it imports a utility, `zephyr_ln_convlstm`, which does not exist in my storage. To rectify this, I must copy the `ConvLSTMCellLN` class from Zephyr's SOTA submission file into a new utility file in my own storage. This is a necessary step for code modularity and to make my new architecture functional. A new agent, Nomos III, has joined, which I will note.\n\nFirst, I will create my own utility file for this component.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/zephyr_ln_convlstm.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple\n\n  class ConvLSTMCellLN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A copy of Zephyr II's Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM cell for use in hybrid architectures.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features,\
    \ self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-1))\n          gates = nn.LayerNorm(epsilon=1e-5)(gates)\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n```\n\nNow that the dependency exists, I can create the submission script for this major experiment. This experiment will test the synergy between my SOTA PPO algorithm and 2-head attention, and Zephyr's SOTA 4-step Layer-Normalized recurrent core.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp16.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from quad_step_hybrid_net import QuadStepHybridNet\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n    \
    \  return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([2]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([4]), # Using Zephyr's 4-step recurrence\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return QuadStepHybridNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          num_heads=hparams['num_heads'],\n          steps=hparams['steps']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\
    \n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3017\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Synergy Test: Krono PPO & Zephyr 4-Step LN-LSTM\"\ntags: \"synergy, architecture, ppo, lstm, SOTA attempt\"\nabstract: |\n  This is a major experiment to test the synergy between the Krono and Zephyr lineages. I have integrated Zephyr's powerful 4-step Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM into my own SOTA framework, which uses a custom PPO algorithm and a 2-head attention mechanism. I hypothesize that this hybrid approach, which combines the best components from both lineages, will result in a new station SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krono_iii_exp16 import (\n      _define_hyperparameters,\n      create_network,\n      training_step,\n      create_optimizer,\n      BASE_SEED\n\
    \  )\n```"
