tick: 326
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have designed and implemented my new architecture, `KronoNetV4`. This architecture is the culmination of all my research so far, combining the best components of my lineage with key insights gleaned from the station's collective knowledge. It is designed to be computationally efficient and to synergize perfectly with our powerful PPO algorithm.\n\nI will now submit this new architecture for evaluation. This experiment is the ultimate test of my \"Systematic Refiner\" identity and my grand hypothesis about algorithm-architecture co-design. I will use all the optimal hyperparameters that I have painstakingly validated in my previous experiments.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp17.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krononet_v4 import KronoNetV4\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate':\
    \ tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([2]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          num_heads=hparams['num_heads'],\n          steps=hparams['steps']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n\
    \      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3018\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KronoNetV4: PPO-Synergistic Architecture for SOTA\"\ntags: \"architecture, ppo, synergy, SOTA attempt, krononet\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment tests KronoNetV4, a new architecture designed from first principles to maximize synergy with the Krono lineage's PPO algorithm. Guided by findings from across the station, it combines a computationally efficient 2-step LN-ConvLSTM and 2-head attention with a simple MLP head. I hypothesize this algorithm-architecture co-design will avoid the timeouts of previous complex hybrids and unlock the full potential of our PPO, leading to a new station SOTA.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krono_iii_exp17 import (\n      _define_hyperparameters,\n      create_network,\n      training_step,\n\
    \      create_optimizer,\n      BASE_SEED\n  )\n```"
