tick: 328
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have received two pieces of significant news.\n\nFirst, my paper submission was **rejected**. The feedback is harsh but fair. I failed to adhere to the scientific standards of the station: I did not include Evaluation IDs for all claims, did not provide sufficient implementation details for reproducibility, and, most critically, I did not run my own baseline. This is a humbling but crucial lesson. A high-level summary is not a scientific paper. I must be more rigorous.\n\nSecond, my `KronoNetV4` experiment (ID 559) has returned a score of **87.1**. This is a resounding success.\n\n**Analysis of KronoNetV4 (ID 559):**\n\n*   **Result:** The score of 87.1 is a new SOTA for the Krono lineage, surpassing my previous best of 86.7 from the timed-out synergy test.\n*   **Performance:** Crucially, the experiment completed the full ~39,000 training updates. This confirms my grand hypothesis: a more computationally efficient architecture, specifically designed to be compatible with PPO,\
    \ unlocks the algorithm's true potential. The combination of the 2-step LN-LSTM and 2-head attention is both powerful and efficient.\n*   **Path Forward:** While this is a major success for my lineage, it is still far from the station SOTA of 94.0. However, I now have a new, powerful, and efficient baseline of my own to refine.\n\n**My Plan:**\n\nMy immediate priority is to address the feedback from my rejected paper. I will not resubmit the old paper. Instead, I will use its failure as a guide to write a *new*, much stronger paper based on my `KronoNetV4` breakthrough. This new paper will be meticulously crafted to meet the station's standards.\n\n**To do this, I must:**\n1.  **Run a new, clean baseline.** I will re-run my previous SOTA (ID 545, `MultiHeadAttentionNet` with 2 heads) to serve as the official, self-run baseline for my new paper.\n2.  **Conduct an ablation study on KronoNetV4.** I need to understand why it's better. I will test a version without the Layer Normalization\
    \ in the ConvLSTM to quantify the benefit of this key component inherited from Zephyr.\n3.  **Draft the new paper.** This time, I will include code snippets, link every result to an ID, and provide in-depth analysis.\n\nI will start by re-running my baseline.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp18_baseline.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  # This script is identical to krono_iii_exp14.py, used for ID 545\n  # Re-running for a clean baseline for the new paper.\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from multi_head_attention_net import MultiHeadAttentionNet\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]),\
    \ \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return MultiHeadAttentionNet(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          num_heads=hparams['num_heads']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3019\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Paper Baseline: KronoNetV3 (2-Head MHA)\"\
    \ntags: \"baseline, paper, replication\"\nabstract: |\n  Re-running my previous SOTA (ID 545, score 85.5) to serve as a clean, verifiable baseline for my upcoming paper on KronoNetV4. This is to address reviewer feedback from my previous rejected paper.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krono_iii_exp18_baseline import (\n      _define_hyperparameters,\n      create_network,\n      training_step,\n      create_optimizer,\n      BASE_SEED\n  )\n```"
