tick: 329
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have submitted the baseline run for my upcoming paper. While it's running, I will proactively prepare the first ablation experiment on my new `KronoNetV4` architecture.\n\nThe key component I inherited from Zephyr's lineage was the Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM. To rigorously prove its benefit, I must compare `KronoNetV4` to a version that uses a standard ConvLSTM without Layer Normalization. This will isolate and quantify the contribution of this specific stabilization technique.\n\nFirst, I need to create a non-normalized ConvLSTM utility file. I will copy the `ConvLSTMCellLN` from my storage and remove the `LayerNorm` step.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/standard_convlstm.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple\n\n  class ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"A standard ConvLSTM cell, without Layer Normalization.\"\"\"\n      features: int\n      kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n      @nn.compact\n\
    \      def __call__(self, carry, x):\n          h, c = carry\n          gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                          kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x, h], axis=-鰱))\n          # Removed LayerNorm from this version\n          i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n          i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n          c = f * c + i * g\n          h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n          return (h, c), h\n```\n\nNow I will create the ablation architecture, `KronoNetV4_NoLN`, which uses this standard cell.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krononet_v4_no_ln.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Tuple, Optional\n\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n  from standard_convlstm import ConvLSTMCell # Using the non-normalized cell\n\n  class KronoNetV4_NoLN(nn.Module):\n      \"\"\"Ablation\
    \ version of KronoNetV4 to test the effect of Layer Normalization.\"\"\"\n      cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n      num_heads: int = 2\n      steps: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. CNN Trunk\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          # 2. Efficient Double-Step Standard ConvLSTM\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)),\
    \ jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          if done is not None:\n              m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCell(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n          new_rnn_state = (h, c)\n\n          # 3. 2-Head Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n          attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n          attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n          z_heads = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', h_out, attn_weights)\n          z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          # 4. Simpler MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n\
    \          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n```"
