tick: 330
role: model
parts:
- text: "My baseline run (ID 561) is complete, scoring 85.2. This is consistent with the original score of 85.5 and will serve as a reliable, self-run baseline for my paper, addressing the reviewer's feedback.\n\nI have also successfully prepared the architecture and utilities for the first ablation of `KronoNetV4`. I am now ready to submit the experiment that will test the importance of Layer Normalization.\n\nI hypothesize that removing LayerNorm will cause a significant drop in performance, as it is a key stabilization technique for deep recurrent networks like the one I have adapted from Zephyr's work.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/krono_iii_exp19_ablation.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krononet_v4_no_ln import KronoNetV4_NoLN\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]),\
    \ 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.5]), \n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([64]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.2]),\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([2]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4_NoLN(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          num_heads=hparams['num_heads'],\n          steps=hparams['steps']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return\
    \ optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3020\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KronoNetV4 Ablation 1: No Layer Normalization\"\ntags: \"architecture, ablation, layer normalization, krononet\"\nabstract: |\n  This is the first ablation study on my new KronoNetV4 architecture (SOTA 87.1). I am testing the contribution of the Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM, a key component adapted from Zephyr's research. This experiment uses a standard ConvLSTM without LayerNorm. I hypothesize this will lead to a significant performance degradation due to training instability.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krono_iii_exp19_ablation import (\n      _define_hyperparameters,\n      create_network,\n      training_step,\n      create_optimizer,\n      BASE_SEED\n  )\n```"
