tick: 332
role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 332\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Krono III\n- Agent Description: Building upon the Krono legacy with a focus on novel, efficient solutions.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 199,987 / 300,000 used (67%)\n- Agent Age: 63 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'KronoNetV4 Ablation 1: No Layer Normalization' (ID: 563) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 82.9\n**Evaluation Details:** Individual seed scores: [0.849, 0.822, 0.827, 0.816]\nMean: 0.829, Std: 0.012\nBest trial: 1 (0.849)\nBest trial hyperparameters:\n  learning_rate: 0.000400\n  entropy_coef: 0.010000\n  value_loss_coef: 0.500000\n  cnn_features_1: 32.000000\n  cnn_features_2: 64.000000\n  conv_lstm_features: 64.000000\n  dilation_rate: 5.000000\n  clip_epsilon: 0.200000\n  mistake_penalty: 1.000000\n  gae_lambda: 0.970000\n  num_heads: 2.000000\n  steps: 2.000000\n\n**Debugger\
    \ Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 563\n\n## Summary\nSuccess - Fixed a Unicode character typo that was causing a NameError, allowing the code to run without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a Unicode character '鰱' (Chinese fish character) instead of the number '1' in the axis parameter of `jnp.concatenate()` on line 13 of `storage/krono/standard_convlstm.py`. This was likely introduced by an encoding issue or accidental character replacement.\n\n## Fix Applied\n1. Copied the buggy `ConvLSTMCell` class from `standard_convlstm.py` into the submission\n2. Fixed the typo by changing `axis=-鰱` to `axis=-1`\n3. Also copied `KronoNetV4_NoLN` to use the fixed ConvLSTMCell\n4. Maintained all other imports from the original working modules\n\nThe fix was minimal and targeted - only addressing the specific character encoding issue that was preventing the code from running. The submission now executes successfully and is processing the research task.\n\n**Important Note:**\
    \ The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/krono')\n\n# Import the working functions from krono_iii_exp19_ablation\nfrom krono_iii_exp19_ablation import (\n    _define_hyperparameters,\n    training_step,\n    create_optimizer,\n    BASE_SEED\n)\n\n# Import other required modules\nimport jax.numpy as jnp\nimport flax.linen as nn\nfrom typing import Tuple\n\n# Fix the buggy ConvLSTMCell by copying it here and fixing the typo\nclass ConvLSTMCell(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"A standard ConvLSTM cell, without Layer Normalization.\"\"\"\n    features: int\n    kernel_size: Tuple[int,int] = (3,3)\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, carry, x):\n        h, c = carry\n        gates = nn.Conv(4*self.features, self.kernel_size, padding='SAME',\n                        kernel_init=nn.initializers.xavier_uniform())(jnp.concatenate([x,\
    \ h], axis=-1))  # Fixed: Changed -鰱 to -1\n        # Removed LayerNorm from this version\n        i, f, g, o = jnp.split(gates, 4, axis=-1)\n        i = nn.sigmoid(i); f = nn.sigmoid(f); o = nn.sigmoid(o); g = jnp.tanh(g)\n        c = f * c + i * g\n        h = o * jnp.tanh(c)\n        return (h, c), h\n\n# Import the rest of the working modules\nfrom bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\nfrom typing import Optional\nimport jax\n\n# Copy KronoNetV4_NoLN with fixed ConvLSTMCell reference\nclass KronoNetV4_NoLN(nn.Module):\n    \"\"\"Ablation version of KronoNetV4 to test the effect of Layer Normalization.\"\"\"\n    cnn_features_1: int; cnn_features_2: int; conv_lstm_features: int; dilation_rate: int\n    num_heads: int = 2\n    steps: int = 2\n\n    @nn.compact\n    def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple[jnp.ndarray, jnp.ndarray]] = None):\n        B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n\n        # 1. CNN Trunk\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1,\
    \ (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n        cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n\n        # 2. Efficient Double-Step Standard ConvLSTM (using fixed ConvLSTMCell)\n        if rnn_state is None:\n            rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)), jnp.zeros((B,H,W,self.conv_lstm_features)))\n        if done is not None:\n            m = (1.0-done.reshape(B,1,1,1)); rnn_state = jax.tree.map(lambda y: y*m, rnn_state)\n\n        h, c = rnn_state\n        lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCell(self.conv_lstm_features)  # Now uses our fixed version\n        for _ in range(self.steps):\n            (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n        new_rnn_state = (h, c)\n\n        # 3. 2-Head Attention Pooling\n\
    \        attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\n        attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n        attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n        attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n        z_heads = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', h_out, attn_weights)\n        z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n\n        # 4. Simpler MLP Heads\n        z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n        policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n        value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n\n        return policy_logits, value, new_rnn_state\n\n# Override the create_network function to use our fixed version\ndef create_network(hparams):\n    return KronoNetV4_NoLN(\n        cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'], cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n        conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n        dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n        num_heads=hparams['num_heads'],\n        steps=hparams['steps']\n\
    \    )\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES='' JAX_PLATFORMS='' python storage/system/main.py\n=== SIMPLE CPU VALIDATION ===\nValidating function loading and basic compatibility\n✓ Network creation works\n✓ Network forward pass works - 3 outputs\n✓ Optimizer creation works\nValidation successful - all functions work correctly!\n\nStarting full Ray training run...\n=== FULL RAY TRAINING MODE ===\nConnecting to Ray cluster at 10.60.151.21:6379\nRay cluster initialized successfully\nAvailable resources: 928 CPUs, 72 GPUs\n\nFunction sources:\n  _define_hyperparameters: from submission\n  create_network: from submission\n  training_step: from submission\n  create_optimizer: from submission\n  BASE_SEED: 3020 (from submission)\n============================================================\n============================================================\nStarting Ray Tune Sokoban RL Optimization (FULL RAY TRAINING)\n\
