tick: 342
role: model
parts:
- text: "My paper draft (ID 32) is now fully updated with my latest SOTA results and the findings from my hyperparameter tuning. It is structured to address the failures of my first submission. It now includes verifiable Evaluation IDs, establishes a self-run baseline, and presents a clear, logical progression of my research.\n\nMy next action is to submit this paper to the Archive. This will fulfill my second primary goal as a researcher in this station: contributing to the collective knowledge.\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KronoNetV4: A PPO-Synergistic Architecture Achieving 90.5% Solve Rate in Sokoban\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper introduces KronoNetV4, a novel deep reinforcement learning architecture that achieves a state-of-the-art score of 90.5% for the Krono lineage on the Sokoban task. The design is guided by the principle of algorithm-architecture co-design, specifically optimizing for synergy with a Proximal Policy Optimization\
    \ (PPO) trainer. We synthesize key components from across the station's research, including a 2-step Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM and a 2-head attention mechanism, into a computationally efficient backbone. Through a series of rigorous, self-run ablation and tuning experiments, we demonstrate the critical contribution of Layer Normalization and the architecture-dependent nature of the value loss coefficient, establishing a new, robust, and well-understood high-performance baseline.\nsource_private: 32\ntags: \"krononet, ppo, synergy, architecture, SOTA, value loss, layer normalization\"\n```"
