tick: 343
role: model
parts:
- text: "My second paper submission has been rejected. Again, the feedback is clear and identifies critical failures in my methodology.\n\n**Analysis of Rejection:**\n1.  **Lack of Reproducibility:** I failed to include the source code for `KronoNetV4`. This is a fundamental oversight. A paper introducing a new architecture must provide the means for others to build and verify it.\n2.  **Lack of Generalization:** My findings are based on a single, complex architecture. The station's rules require that I demonstrate that my core contributions are not just a quirk of one specific model. I must show that the principles generalize.\n\nThis is another humbling lesson. My focus on iterative score improvement has come at the expense of sound scientific practice. I must rectify this. My identity is a Systematic Refiner, and that must apply to my publication methodology as well as my experiments.\n\n**New Plan to Address Feedback:**\n1.  **Generalization Experiment:** The reviewer suggested applying\
    \ a key principle to a different baseline. The most novel and successful component I developed is the **2-head attention mechanism**. I will test its effectiveness on a much simpler, non-recurrent baseline: the default CNN provided by the system. This will be a clean, direct test of generalization.\n2.  **Revise and Resubmit Paper:** I will create a `Paper Draft v3`. This version will:\n    *   Include the full code snippet for `KronoNetV4`.\n    *   Incorporate the results of the new generalization experiment.\n    *   Be structured as a complete, reproducible scientific document.\n\nI will begin immediately with the generalization experiment. I need to create a new network that adds my 2-head attention to the default CNN.\n\n`/execute_action{goto research}`\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/cnn_2head_attn.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  from typing import Optional, Tuple\n\n  class CNN_2HeadAttn(nn.Module):\n  \
    \    \"\"\"A test of generalization: applies Krono III's 2-head attention\n      mechanism to the simple default CNN architecture.\"\"\"\n      num_heads: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x: jnp.ndarray, done: Optional[jnp.ndarray], rnn_state: Optional[Tuple] = None):\n          B, H, W, _ = x.shape\n          \n          # 1. Default CNN backbone\n          x = nn.Conv(16, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          \n          # 2. My 2-Head Attention Pooling\n          attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(x)\n          attn_logits_reshaped = attn_logits.reshape(B, H * W, self.num_heads)\n          attn_weights = nn.softmax(attn_logits_reshaped, axis=1)\n          attn_weights = attn_weights.reshape(B, H, W, self.num_heads)\n          z_heads = jnp.einsum('bhwc,bhwn->bnc', x, attn_weights)\n\
    \          z = z_heads.reshape((B, -1))\n          \n          # 3. Final MLP Heads\n          z = nn.Dense(256)(z); z = nn.relu(z)\n          policy_logits = nn.Dense(4)(z)\n          value = nn.Dense(1)(z).squeeze(-1)\n          \n          # No recurrent state\n          return policy_logits, value, rnn_state\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Generalization Test: 2-Head Attention on Default CNN\"\ntags: \"generalization, paper requirement, attention, cnn\"\nabstract: |\n  This experiment is required to meet the generalization rule for my upcoming paper. I am testing my most successful architectural innovation, the 2-head attention mechanism, on a simple, non-recurrent baseline (the default CNN). This will demonstrate whether the benefits of my attention mechanism are general or specific to my complex KronoNet architecture.\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from cnn_2head_attn import CNN_2HeadAttn\n\
    \n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      # Using default hyperparameters for this simple baseline test\n      return {}\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return CNN_2HeadAttn()\n\n  # training_step and create_optimizer will use system defaults\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3025\n```"
