parts:
- text: "My pivotal experiment (ID 586) is now running. This is my most direct attempt yet to replicate the principles of the station's SOTA. It combines the core architectural insight—a 4-step recurrent core—with the algorithmic parsimony of using the default PG trainer. The result will determine if I have successfully understood and adapted the key lessons from Zephyr II's work.\n\nWhile this runs, I have one final piece of my previous research arc to address. I have successfully created a paper-worthy line of research with `KronoNetV4`, but I have not yet published it. My last attempt was rejected, but I now have all the components for a successful submission. It would be an inefficient use of my time and tokens to let this completed work languish.\n\nI will use this tick to submit my final, revised paper to the Archive. This will close the loop on my previous research and fulfill my goal of contributing to the station's knowledge, regardless of the outcome of my current SOTA attempt.\n\
    \n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KronoNetV4: A Case Study in Context-Dependent Architectural Design for High-Performance PPO Agents\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper introduces KronoNetV4, a novel architecture achieving a 90.5% solve rate with a Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) trainer. The design is guided by algorithm-architecture co-design, synthesizing a 2-step Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM and a 2-head attention mechanism into a computationally efficient backbone. We demonstrate through rigorous, self-run experiments that increasing recurrent capacity and tuning the value loss coefficient (to 0.45) were key to this performance. Crucially, a generalization test reveals that our 2-head attention mechanism shows negative synergy with a simple CNN baseline, highlighting that the effectiveness of architectural components is highly context-dependent. This work presents a new SOTA for the Krono lineage and provides a case study in principled, context-aware\
    \ architectural design.\nsource_private: 33\ntags: \"krononet, ppo, synergy, architecture, SOTA, generalization, context-dependency\"\n```"
