parts:
- text: "My second attempt at the mechanistic probe has failed again. This time the error is `flax.errors.CallCompactUnboundModuleError`. This is a more subtle error related to how Flax handles `nn.Module` methods. My approach of defining a helper method and then monkey-patching it onto the class is flawed and incompatible with how Flax's `@nn.compact` decorator works.\n\nI must redesign the probe. Instead of trying to cleverly extract backbone features from my existing `nn.Module` classes, I will create new, dedicated `nn.Module` classes for each backbone. This is a cleaner, more robust approach that will avoid the Flax error.\n\n**Plan:**\n1.  Create a `SimpleCNNBackbone` module.\n2.  Create a `KronoNetV4Backbone` module.\n3.  Rewrite the `test()` function to use these new, dedicated modules.\n4.  Resubmit the probe.\n\nThe Archive cooldown persists, so this remains my most productive course of action.\n\n`/execute_action{storage write krono/mechanistic_probe_v3.py}`\n```yaml\ncontent:\
    \ |\n  import sys\n  import jax\n  import jax.numpy as jnp\n  import flax.linen as nn\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from bottleneck_sota import BottleneckBlock\n  from zephyr_ln_convlstm import ConvLSTMCellLN\n\n  # New, dedicated module for the simple CNN backbone\n  class SimpleCNNBackbone(nn.Module):\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x):\n          x = nn.Conv(16, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          x = nn.Conv(32, (3,3), padding='SAME')(x); x = nn.relu(x)\n          return x\n\n  # New, dedicated module for the KronoNetV4 backbone\n  class KronoNetV4Backbone(nn.Module):\n      cnn_features_1: int = 32\n      cnn_features_2: int = 64\n      conv_lstm_features: int = 96\n      dilation_rate: int = 5\n      steps: int = 2\n\n      @nn.compact\n      def __call__(self, x, done=None, rnn_state=None):\n          if rnn_state is None:\n              rnn_state = (jnp.zeros((x.shape[0],\
    \ 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features)), \n                           jnp.zeros((x.shape[0], 8, 8, self.conv_lstm_features)))\n          \n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_1, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(x); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_1)(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = nn.Conv(self.cnn_features_2, (3,3), padding='SAME', kernel_dilation=self.dilation_rate)(cnn_out); cnn_out = nn.relu(cnn_out)\n          cnn_out = BottleneckBlock(self.cnn_features_2)(cnn_out)\n          \n          h, c = rnn_state\n          lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n          for _ in range(self.steps):\n              (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n          return h_out\n\n  def test():\n      \"\"\"\n      A mechanistic probe (v3) to test the reviewer's hypothesis.\n      Uses dedicated, clean nn.Module classes for each backbone.\n      \"\"\"\n      print(\"--- Starting Mechanistic Probe\
    \ (v3) ---\")\n      key = jax.random.PRNGKey(0)\n      dummy_input = jnp.zeros((1, 8, 8, 8))\n\n      # --- Model 1: Simple CNN Backbone ---\n      cnn_backbone = SimpleCNNBackbone()\n      cnn_params = cnn_backbone.init(key, dummy_input)['params']\n      cnn_features = cnn_backbone.apply({'params': cnn_params}, dummy_input)\n      cnn_variance = jnp.mean(jnp.var(cnn_features, axis=-1))\n      print(f\"Simple CNN Backbone: Mean Channel Variance = {cnn_variance:.6f}\")\n\n      # --- Model 2: KronoNetV4 Backbone ---\n      kn4_backbone = KronoNetV4Backbone()\n      kn4_params = kn4_backbone.init(key, dummy_input)['params']\n      kn4_features = kn4_backbone.apply({'params': kn4_params}, dummy_input)\n      kn4_variance = jnp.mean(jnp.var(kn4_features, axis=-1))\n      print(f\"KronoNetV4 Backbone: Mean Channel Variance = {kn4_variance:.6f}\")\n      \n      return f\"Probe Complete. Variances: CNN={cnn_variance:.6f}, KronoNetV4={kn4_variance:.6f}\"\n```\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n\
    ```yaml\ntitle: \"Mechanistic Probe v3: Feature Variance (Flax Fix)\"\ntags: \"probe, analysis, test-only, paper requirement, variance, debug\"\nabstract: |\n  Third attempt at my mechanistic probe, this time with a robust implementation that avoids Flax's UnboundModuleError. I have created new, dedicated nn.Module classes for each backbone to ensure a clean and correct execution. The probe will provide a mechanistic explanation for the context-dependent performance of my 2-head attention mechanism by comparing feature variance.\ncontent: |\n  import sys\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from mechanistic_probe_v3 import test\n```"
