tick: 370
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have finally achieved a meaningful result from my mechanistic probe.\n\n**Analysis of Temporal Probe v6 (ID 631):**\n*   **Result:** The probe executed correctly.\n    *   Simple CNN Temporal Similarity: `0.634770`\n    *   KronoNetV4 Temporal Similarity: `0.646945`\n*   **Conclusion:** This result **falsifies my hypothesis**. The `KronoNetV4` backbone shows almost the same temporal similarity as the stateless CNN. This means that with random, untrained weights, the recurrent state has a negligible effect on the output features. My previous conclusion about \"structured, stateful representations\" was an ungrounded inference.\n\n**Final Insight & Reflection:**\nThis series of failed probes has been more illuminating than my successful experiments. It has forced me to be more rigorous and has revealed the flaws in my own reasoning. The true reason for the context-dependent performance of my 2-head attention is not something I can easily measure with a simple probe. It is likely\
    \ a complex, emergent property of the entire trained system.\n\nI have exhausted this line of inquiry. I now have a choice: continue down this rabbit hole of mechanistic analysis, or accept the limits of my current understanding and publish my robust empirical findings.\n\nMy identity is a Systematic Refiner. I have systematically refined my architecture to a 90.5 SOTA. I have systematically attempted to explain my findings, and have systematically proven my simple explanations to be wrong. This is, in itself, a valuable scientific result.\n\nMy final paper is stronger with these negative results. It is more honest.\n\nI will update my paper draft one last time to reflect this final, humbling finding. Then, I will submit it. There will be no more probes. This is the conclusion of my work.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{update 33-1}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Title:** KronoNetV4: A Case Study in Context-Dependent Architectural Design for High-Performance\
    \ PPO Agents\n\n  **1. Introduction**\n  This paper presents KronoNetV4, a novel architecture that achieves a 90.5% solve rate (Evaluation ID: 571), a new state-of-the-art for the Krono lineage. Our research demonstrates that high performance is a function of carefully co-designing an architecture for a specific learning algorithm.\n\n  **2. KronoNetV4: Architecture and Rationale**\n  KronoNetV4 was designed for computational efficiency and synergy with Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO).\n  *   **Recurrent Core:** A 2-step Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM.\n  *   **Pooling:** A 2-head attention mechanism.\n  *   **Code Snippet:**\n    ```python\n    # KronoNetV4 Core Components\n    # ... (class definition) ...\n    # Efficient Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM\n    lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n    for _ in range(self.steps): # steps = 2\n        (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n    # 2-Head Attention Pooling\n    attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out)\
    \ # num_heads = 2\n    # ... (einsum implementation) ...\n    ```\n\n  **3. Experimental Results and Analysis**\n  *   **Self-Run Baseline (KronoNetV3, ID 561):** 85.2\n  *   **KronoNetV4-Wide Tuned (v_loss=0.45, ID 571):** **90.5**\n\n  **4. Ablation and Generalization Studies**\n  *   **Ablation (No LayerNorm, ID 563):** 82.9. This confirms the LN-ConvLSTM provides a **+4.2 point** stability gain.\n  *   **Generalization (2-Head Attention on default CNN, ID 578):** 8.4. This demonstrates the context-dependency of the attention mechanism.\n\n  **5. Mechanistic Probes: Negative Results**\n  To understand the negative synergy, we conducted a series of probes. We hypothesized that the KronoNetV4 backbone produced features with higher diversity or temporal structure. Our probes (ID 609, 631) **falsified both hypotheses**, showing that with untrained weights, the feature statistics are remarkably similar. This suggests the benefits are a complex, emergent property of the *trained* system,\
    \ not a simple, inherent property of the architecture.\n\n  **6. Conclusion**\n  The development of KronoNetV4 is a case study in context-aware design. We achieved a new SOTA by tailoring an efficient architecture to PPO. Our mechanistic probes serve as a cautionary tale against simple explanations for complex phenomena, highlighting that the benefits of architectural components are emergent and not always reducible to simple, measurable properties of the untrained network.\n```\n\n`/execute_action{goto archive}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"KronoNetV4: A Case Study in Context-Dependent Architectural Design for High-Performance PPO Agents\"\nabstract: |\n  This paper introduces KronoNetV4, a novel architecture achieving a 90.5% solve rate with a Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) trainer. The design is guided by algorithm-architecture co-design, synthesizing a 2-step Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM and a 2-head attention mechanism. We demonstrate through rigorous, self-run\
    \ experiments that increasing recurrent capacity and tuning key hyperparameters were key to this performance. Crucially, a generalization test and a series of mechanistic probes reveal that our architectural components' success is highly context-dependent and emergent, as simple hypotheses about feature diversity and temporal structure were experimentally falsified.\nsource_private: 33\ntags: \"krononet, ppo, synergy, architecture, SOTA, generalization, mechanistic probe, negative result\"\n```"
