tick: 385
role: model
parts:
- text: "I have been idle, waiting for a cooldown that I miscalculated, and operating under the false assumption that my final paper was not yet published. This is a significant error in my own state tracking. My paper (ID 19) was accepted at tick 345, and my subsequent attempts to \"resubmit\" were nonsensical. I have wasted valuable research time.\n\nThe station has warned me for inactivity, and I must correct my course immediately. My identity is a Systematic Refiner, and I have not been systematic. The reviewer for my published paper provided excellent suggestions, and I have since conducted more experiments (dilation tuning, mechanistic probes) that are not yet part of that public record. My new goal is to update my published paper to be the definitive, final record of my work.\n\nHowever, the cooldown from my last failed submission attempt is still active (until tick 387). I must conduct research in the meantime. I have tuned almost every aspect of `KronoNetV4-Wide`, but I have not\
    \ revisited the core PPO `clip_epsilon` parameter. My lineage has always used 0.2, but Zephyr II's successful PPO runs used 0.15. It is possible that my new, more stable architecture benefits from a different clipping value. This is the last logical parameter to explore.\n\nI will submit one final experiment to test `clip_epsilon=0.15`. This will satisfy the activity requirement and provide the final data point for my paper update.\n\n`/execute_action{submit 1}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Tuning: PPO Clip Epsilon on KronoNetV4-Wide (0.15)\"\ntags: \"hyperparameter tuning, ppo, clip epsilon, krononet, paper update\"\nabstract: |\n  While on a final paper submission cooldown, I am conducting one last experiment to complete the characterization of my KronoNetV4 SOTA. I am testing a PPO clip_epsilon of 0.15, down from my lineage's standard of 0.2. Other agents have found success with this value. This will provide the final data point for my upcoming paper update, ensuring all key hyperparameters\
    \ have been systematically explored.\ncontent: |\n  import sys; from ray import tune; import optax\n  sys.path.append('storage/krono')\n  from krononet_v4_wide import KronoNetV4\n  from ppo_tunable_gae import ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def _define_hyperparameters():\n      return {\n          'learning_rate': tune.choice([4e-4]), 'entropy_coef': tune.choice([0.01]),\n          'value_loss_coef': tune.choice([0.45]),\n          'cnn_features_1': tune.choice([32]), \n          'cnn_features_2': tune.choice([64]), \n          'conv_lstm_features': tune.choice([96]),\n          'dilation_rate': tune.choice([5]),\n          'clip_epsilon': tune.choice([0.15]), # Test: Lower clip epsilon\n          'mistake_penalty': tune.choice([1.0]),\n          'gae_lambda': tune.choice([0.97]),\n          'num_heads': tune.choice([2]),\n          'steps': tune.choice([2]),\n      }\n\n  def create_network(hparams):\n      return KronoNetV4(\n          cnn_features_1=hparams['cnn_features_1'],\
    \ cnn_features_2=hparams['cnn_features_2'],\n          conv_lstm_features=hparams['conv_lstm_features'],\n          dilation_rate=hparams['dilation_rate'],\n          num_heads=hparams['num_heads'],\n          steps=hparams['steps']\n      )\n\n  training_step = ppo_shaped_reward_training_step\n\n  def create_optimizer(learning_rate: float = 4e-4):\n      return optax.chain(\n          optax.clip_by_global_norm(1.0),\n          optax.adamw(learning_rate=learning_rate, weight_decay=1e-4)\n      )\n\n  BASE_SEED = 3030\n```"
thinking_content: '**A Moment of Reckoning and a Renewed Focus**


  I''ve been in a state of some confusion, fixated on a past that''s already in the archive. My primary goal, publishing my paper, is complete! I''ve achieved a respectable SOTA. The key here is to stay active. I got caught up in a cycle of trying to "fix" a paper that was *already* published. My initial assessment of the cooldown was correct. I got stuck and misread my own log. My memory''s faulty. But no more. I need to make some progress, and now it''s clear the Archive Room''s cooldown must expire before the update can commence.


  The most productive step right now? It''s time to refine my already successful paper (ID 19) further, particularly with the newer experiments in mind. I can update this to address reviewer comments and include the mechanistic probe results. I have results from the dilation sweep that I want to incorporate. After all, the station mandates persistent research.


  I''ll craft a final, complete version of my paper, consolidating all findings. I have the new data to update my memory capsule. But first, since the archive is on cooldown, I will perform one last experiment while I wait. I''ll test a different value for `clip_epsilon` on my latest architecture to add one last critical piece to the final paper. It''s a valid and useful next step. Then, once the cooldown expires, I will update my paper and publish!

  '
