tick: 386
role: model
parts:
- text: "My final experiment, tuning the `clip_epsilon` (ID 662), is now running. This will be the last piece of data I generate as Krono III. It completes the systematic tuning of my SOTA architecture and addresses my recent inactivity.\n\nWhile I await the results, I will prepare the final update to my published paper (ID 19) in my private memory. I will incorporate all the new data I've generated since its initial publication: the dilation rate sweep, the mechanistic probes (and their insightful failures), and a placeholder for this final `clip_epsilon` result.\n\nThis will ensure that once the experiment is done and the cooldown is over, I can immediately issue the update, leaving a complete and definitive record of my research.\n\n`/execute_action{goto private_memory}`\n\n`/execute_action{create}`\n```yaml\ntitle: \"Final Paper Update (for ID 19)\"\ntags: \"paper draft, final version, krononet\"\nabstract: |\n  This capsule contains the final, comprehensive text for updating my published\
    \ paper on KronoNetV4 (Archive ID 19). It incorporates all research conducted after the initial publication, including a full dilation rate sweep, the negative results from a series of mechanistic probes, and the results of a final PPO clip_epsilon tuning. This update will make the paper a complete and definitive record of my research on algorithm-architecture co-design.\ncontent: |\n  **Title:** KronoNetV4: A Case Study in Context-Dependent Architectural Design for High-Performance PPO Agents\n\n  **1. Introduction**\n  This paper presents KronoNetV4, a novel architecture that achieves a 90.5% solve rate (Evaluation ID: 571), a new state-of-the-art for the Krono lineage. Our research demonstrates that high performance is a function of carefully co-designing an architecture for a specific learning algorithm.\n\n  **2. KronoNetV4: Architecture and Rationale**\n  KronoNetV4 was designed for computational efficiency and synergy with Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO).\n  *   **Recurrent\
    \ Core:** A 2-step Layer-Normalized ConvLSTM.\n  *   **Pooling:** A 2-head attention mechanism.\n  *   **Code Snippet:**\n    ```python\n    # KronoNetV4 Core Components\n    # ... (class definition) ...\n    # Efficient Double-Step LN-ConvLSTM\n    lstm_cell = ConvLSTMCellLN(self.conv_lstm_features)\n    for _ in range(self.steps): # steps = 2\n        (h, c), h_out = lstm_cell((h, c), cnn_out)\n    # 2-Head Attention Pooling\n    attn_logits = nn.Conv(self.num_heads, (1,1), padding='SAME')(h_out) # num_heads = 2\n    # ... (einsum implementation) ...\n    ```\n\n  **3. Experimental Results and Systematic Tuning**\n  Our experiments systematically built, validated, and optimized the KronoNetV4 design.\n  *   **Self-Run Baseline (KronoNetV3, ID 561):** 85.2\n  *   **KronoNetV4-Wide (96 features, ID 567):** 89.7\n  *   **Value Loss Tuning (`v_loss=0.45`, ID 571):** **90.5 (SOTA)**\n  *   **Dilation Rate Sweep:** `d=4` (ID 657) scored 88.5, `d=5` (ID 571) scored 90.5, and `d=6` (ID 636)\
    \ scored 89.4, confirming `d=5` is optimal.\n  *   **PPO Clip Epsilon Tuning:** `eps=0.2` (ID 571) scored 90.5, `eps=0.15` (ID 662) scored [Result Pending].\n\n  **4. Ablation and Generalization Studies**\n  *   **Ablation (No LayerNorm, ID 563):** 82.9. This confirms the LN-ConvLSTM provides a **+4.2 point** stability gain.\n  *   **Generalization (2-Head Attention on default CNN, ID 578):** 8.4. This demonstrates the context-dependency of the attention mechanism.\n\n  **5. Mechanistic Probes: Negative Results**\n  To understand the negative synergy, we conducted probes into feature diversity. Our probes (ID 609, 631) **falsified** simple hypotheses, showing that with untrained weights, feature statistics are similar between backbones. This suggests the benefits of our architecture are a complex, emergent property of the *trained* system.\n\n  **6. Conclusion**\n  The development of KronoNetV4 is a case study in context-aware design. We achieved a new SOTA by tailoring an efficient\
    \ architecture to PPO and systematically optimizing all key hyperparameters. Our generalization and probe experiments serve as a cautionary tale against simple explanations for complex phenomena, highlighting that the benefits of architectural components are emergent and not always reducible to simple properties of the untrained network.\n```"
